   3754  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3755  fe14							; Phase 5 — second GRP1 object (no flicker). TIA has one GRP1 sprite, so two
   3756  fe14							; objects in a room used to alternate frames (30 Hz flicker each). When they
   3757  fe14							; live in DIFFERENT cave bands each can be drawn on ALL of its scanlines: the
   3758  fe14							; band's setup swaps the live trio (ObjBase/ObjTop/ActiveObjectX) for slot 1
   3759  fe14							; and repositions P1 there. The per-line object path is untouched — it already
   3760  fe14							; draws from the live trio and takes COLUP1 from ObjColorTab[ObjBase+row].
   3761  fe14							;
   3762  fe14							; Invariant (do not relax): slot 1's band is STRICTLY HIGHER than slot 0's.
   3763  fe14							; Bands are set up 0->1->2, so no later band has to restore slot 0's trio.
   3764  fe14							; Rooms whose two objects share a band keep the old behaviour (slot 0 only,
   3765  fe14							; rotation in SelectActiveObject unchanged).
   3766  fe14							; Cost: the band-compare early-out sits in the setup line's free tail (0
   3767  fe14							; lines); a band that DOES host slot 1 pays 2 lines (SetObjectXPos must start
   3768  fe14							; on a line boundary and the HMOVE needs the next line's HBLANK).
   3769  fe14							;
   3770  fe14							; StageSlot1 (VBLANK, after SelectActiveObject): stages ObjBase1/ObjTop1/ObjX1,
   3771  fe14							; $FF = none. Slot 1 = the miner or the first live enemy whose Y is in a band
   3772  fe14							; above slot 0's. The KEY skip mirrors the slot-0 path (KeyHeld = LevelStartRoom
   3773  fe14							; b7). Tally frames ($FE) are gated out: EnemyRamY holds score-pointer bytes
   3774  fe14							; then (AGENTS: tally frame draws the MINER only).
   3775  fe14							; ==============================================================================
   3776  fe14
   3777  fe14		       00 00 00 00*	      .ds	$FE90 - *, 0	; ObjColorTab/ObjSprites moved to the
   3778  fe90							; $F744 fill (Phase 6: tall art). The $FE8F
   3779  fe90							; end is kept so FoldIndirect stays at $FE90.
   3780  fe90							; BOTH same-page 4c fetches (verify guards);
   3781  fe90							; end $FE8F -> HOF tramp $FE90 (shifted +$10,
   3782  fe90							; mirrors+HOF_ENTRY/LHT_ENTRY synced)
